{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And YHWH will guide you continually.</b> The meaning: He will be with you in every place you go." "<b>In scorched places.</b> Like צחה צמא (Isaiah 5:13), the opposite of watering." "<b>And He will satisfy your bones.</b> Some say it is like ידשן without a comparable, and others said it means יחזק, like חלוצי צבא (Numbers 31:5). Some say it means יחליץ like יחלץ (Job 36:15), as we find ישליח (Exodus 8:17) ישלח (Psalms 78:45), ישמיח [ibid. 89:43] ישמח (Lamentations 2:17), and this is the correct view, for it is like שומר כל עצמותיו (Psalms 34:21), and He will deliver them from breaking." "<b>Not one of them shall be broken.</b> Like יכרתו, and כזב [Psalms 4:3] is from its root, for it is a thing that does not stand, for it is a chance occurrence."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {2 "Resolved [שם פ\"ט מ\"ג] to Psalms 89:43 based on context, as the preceding and following citations are both from Psalms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:12.867787116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}